  "payload": {
    "source": { "id": "259:508", "name": "Icon", "type": "COMPONENT_SET" },
    "description": "The single icon component for the system: one glyph from the DY icon set (Lucide; ISC and MIT, see @dy/icons LICENSE) at one of 5 sizes.\nPURPOSE: Every icon in the UI, on its own or inside a component slot such as Button and Anchor iconLeading / iconTrailing.\nBEHAVIOR: size (xs | s | m | l | xl) maps to dy/size/icon/* (12/16/20/24/32px). The icon property swaps the glyph; only components in the Icons section are valid glyphs. Glyphs are drawn on a 24×24 grid with a 2px stroke, and the stroke scales with size, as an SVG viewBox does in code.\nCOMPOSITION: A square frame holding one glyph instance. No padding, fill or border. Color is the stroke, bound to dy/color/text/default here; in code the glyph uses currentColor and inherits the surrounding text color, so containing components override the color, not Icon.\nUSAGE: Pair an icon with a visible text label whenever possible. Pick the size that matches the adjacent text or the containing component’s size, rather than overriding the frame.\nACCESSIBILITY: Decorative by default: hidden from assistive tech (aria-hidden) because the adjacent label carries the meaning. An icon that conveys meaning on its own takes a label, which renders role=&quot;img&quot; with that accessible name. Never rely on an icon alone for an interactive control’s name.\nCODE GENERATION NOTES: Maps to ONE Icon component in @dy/react. icon takes an icon component from @dy/icons/react (e.g. ChevronDownIcon), never a string name or a ReactNode. size is a prop that selects a --dy-size-icon-* token. Do not emit a component per glyph or per size, and do not inline SVG markup.",
